# Artifact Governance

## Purpose

Use `ARTIFACT_REGISTRY.json` as the machine-readable inventory of retained artifacts for <strong>{{PROJECT_NAME}}</strong>. This bilingual guide records governance rules and notable interpretation boundaries; it does not duplicate every registry item.

## Required classification

Every material item records both:

- <strong>Lifecycle:</strong> `active`, `proposed`, `historical`, `retired`, or `unconfirmed`.
- <strong>Evidence authority:</strong> `authoritative`, `descriptive`, `selection-only`, `reference-only`, or `invalid-for-decisions`.

Existence, a valid path, or a matching hash does not grant decision authority. State the item's validity boundary and replacement when one exists.

## Registry fields

Use a stable `id`, `kind`, explicit locator, lifecycle, authority, provenance, contract or version identity when applicable, fingerprint and fingerprint contract when reproducibility matters, creation time, replacement, and validity boundary.

Never invent hashes, owners, versions, or provenance. Omit unknown optional values or classify the item as unconfirmed.

## Notable boundaries

No project-specific artifact is confirmed during initialization.

## Maintenance

Update the JSON registry when a retained artifact is added, replaced, reclassified, archived, restored, or loses decision authority. Update this guide only when the governance rule or an interpretation boundary changes.
